aration": "homemade or canned", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 7-ounce package Konriko Wild Pecan rice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "7-ounce package konriko wild pecan rice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "3 ounces (1 cup) pecan halves, toasted and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "(1 cup) pecan halves", "preparation": "toasted and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 ½ cups thinly sliced scallions, including green part", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced scallions", "preparation": "including green part", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "12 cherry tomatoes, cut in half", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cherry tomatoes", "preparation": "cut in half", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 large, ripe avocado", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large", "preparation": "ripe avocado", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "Freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To prepare the vinaigrette, place the chick peas, garlic, vinegar and soy sauce in the bowl of a food processor fitted with a steel chopping blade and process into a smooth puree, scraping down the workbowl as necessary."}, {"position": 2, "text": "With the motor running, pour the sesame and vegetable oils through the feed tube in a slow, steady stream. The vinaigrette will be creamy and thick. Scrape into a screw-top glass jar and refrigerate until needed."}, {"position": 3, "text": "For the salad, poach the chicken breasts in the stock until just cooked. Remove from the stock, let cool and cut into three-quarter-inch cubes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Cook the rice according to package directions, making sure all the water has evaporated. Set aside to cool."}, {"position": 5, "text": "In a large bowl, combine the rice, chicken cubes, chopped pecans and scallions. Add the cherry tomatoes. Peel the avocado and cut it into three-quarter-inch cubes, adding it to the salad. Pour on the vinaigrette and toss to blend. Add freshly ground black pepper to taste. Serve on Boston lettuce leaves, if desired."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 509.0, "protein_g": 27.1, "carbohydrates_g": 34.2, "fat_g": 29.8, "saturated_fat_g": 3.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 64.8, "sodium_mg": 395.0, "fiber_g": 5.7, "sugar_g": 4.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 23.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["brunch", "dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": [], "other": ["chicken breast", "chickpea", "grain bowl", "pecan", "poach", "rice", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 12}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1987-09-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:25:11.602632+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "penne-with-artichokes-and-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 11755, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11755-penne-with-artichokes-and-mushrooms", "name": "Penne With Artichokes And Mushrooms", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 tablespoons, plus 2 teaspoons, olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "tablespoons", "preparation": "plus 2 teaspoons, olive oil", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 large shallots, peeled and minced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large shallots", "preparation": "peeled and minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "4 cups stemmed and quartered shiitake mushrooms", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "stemmed and quartered shiitake mushrooms", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 13 ¾-ounce cans artichoke hearts, well drained and quartered", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "13 ¾-ounce cans artichoke hearts", "preparation": "well drained and quartered", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 pound penne", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "penne", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat 2 teaspoons of the olive oil in a large, nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the shallots and cook until softened, about 2 minutes. Add the mushrooms and cook until tender, about 10 minutes. Stir in the artichoke hearts and cook for 2 minutes. Season with the salt and pepper."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, bring a large pot of lightly salted water to the boil. Add the penne and cook just until tender. Drain. Place in a large bowl. Toss in the artichoke mixture and the remaining 2 tablespoons of olive oil. Season with additional salt and pepper if needed. Divide among 4 plates and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 626.4, "protein_g": 23.7, "carbohydrates_g": 117.2, "fat_g": 9.2, "saturated_fat_g": 1.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 783.1, "fiber_g": 17.4, "sugar_g": 9.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 6.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["appetizer", "main course", "side dish"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["artichoke heart", "boil", "easy", "five ingredient", "pasta", "pastas", "quick", "saute"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 68}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-09-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:49:35.153097+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "penne-with-dried-porcini-and-italian-sausage", "nyt_id": 10473, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10473-penne-with-dried-porcini-and-italian-sausage", "name": "Penne With Dried Porcini And Italian Sausage", "author": "Moira Hodgson", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 first-course servings, 4 main-course servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": 30, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 minutes", "cook": "30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ½ ounces dried porcini mushrooms", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "dried porcini mushrooms", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 medium onion, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 clove garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 pound Italian sweet sausage sliced into 1-inch pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "italian sweet sausage sliced into 1-inch pieces", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon tomato paste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tomato paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cups chicken stock", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon fresh rosemary, oregano or thyme leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fresh rosemary", "preparation": "oregano or thyme leaves", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Coarse salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 pound penne", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "penne", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Freshly grated Parmesan cheese", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly grated parmesan cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Soak the mushrooms in one-and-a-half cups hot water for 30 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile saute the onion and the garlic in the olive oil until soft. Add the sausage and brown lightly. Drain off any fat."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Drain the mushroom through a coffee filter or cheesecloth, reserving the soaking liquid. Quickly rinse the mushrooms under the running water."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add the mushrooms with their soaking liquid to the onion, along with the tomato paste, chicken stock and herbs. Season lightly with salt and pepper and simmer gently for half an hour. If the sauce gets too thick add more stock. If it is too thin, turn up the heat."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Meanwhile, bring six quarts water to boil for the penne. Cook the penne, drain and place in a heated bowl. Pour the sauce on top, toss thoroughly and serve immediately. Pass the cheese separately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 464.0, "protein_g": 19.7, "carbohydrates_g": 51.3, "fat_g": 20.0, "saturated_fat_g": 5.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 43.9, "sodium_mg": 567.3, "fiber_g": 2.9, "sugar_g": 3.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 12.1, "source": "nyt", "basis":